Hi all,

I'm Sartak (aka Eidolos, as many of you know me) the primary author of
TAEB. Sorry for not discussing the bot with you all sooner - there's
always a desire to make it better before showing it off to people.

The reason that TAEB plays so slowly is because there's a massive
amount of indirection in every component. The biggest costs seem to be
in pathfinding. We're always working to improve his play speed. A
competitor bot, saiph, is actually faster than NetHack itself, and I'm
incredibly jealous of what that has given them. The only intentional
delay is in making sure we've collected all output from NetHack (which
turns out to be a very tricky problem).

There are two AIs for TAEB (its AI is pluggable - the framework,
called TAEB, just asks the AI what to do each turn). Most of the TAEB
authors hack and use the "Behavioral" AI. There's another hacker,
ais523, working on a different AI called "Planar". The names you see
on NAO are usually just the author's name (such as doy running
doytaeb).

If you do IRC, we hang out in #interhack on irc.freenode.org. Swing by
and we'll give you a demo or something! I'll keep an eye on this
thread for any further questions.

